# Behavioral CAPTCHA — Red-Team / Evasion Issue Log

## Issue 001 — Qmodel V0.2 button-sequence evasion (API 91.7% vs Playwright gap)

**Status:** patched (Qmodel V0.3 + API hardening); open (live browser parity)  
**Date:** 2026-08-17  
**Target model:** `qmodel_v0.2` (evaded) → **`qmodel_v0.3`** (patched)  
**Challenge:** `button_sequence`  
**Goal:** ≥70% human confidence, no replay attacks  
**Artifacts:** `test/qmodel_evasion_bot.py`, `test/qmodel_best_result.json`, `test/playwright_button_bot.py`

---

### Summary

A new procedural **wobble/eased-linear** bot evaded Qmodel V0.2 at **91.71%** when events were generated in Python and submitted via the REST API. The same tuned config does **not** transfer to visible Playwright runs because the dashboard scores **live pointer recordings**, not the pre-generated event JSON. Best live Playwright score so far: **60%** (PASSED). Several Playwright approaches scored 0–47%.

---

### Blue-team patch (2026-08-17)

**Qmodel V0.3** (`test/patch_issue001.py`):

- Exported wobble evasion telemetry → `datasets/bot_evasion/evasion_cycle_002.csv`
- Retrained RF with bot_evasion cycles 001+002
- Static heuristics **#9** (broad wobble signature) + **#10** (low-straightness variant) in `backend/model.py`
- Dynamic rule `evasion_cycle_002` in `backend/qmodels/qmodel_v0.3_evasion_rules.json`

**API / dashboard hardening** (`backend/challenge_security.py`, `CAPTCHA_STRICT=1` default):

- Session-bound `verify_token`, `source: "dashboard"` required
- Pointer attestation (`pid` from canvas PointerEvents)
- Wall-clock vs telemetry duration checks (blocks instant JSON inject)
- `/api/verify` and `/api/simulate-bot` disabled in strict mode
- Dashboard records `pid`, `pt`, `src` on canvas events

**Post-patch wobble bot vs V0.3 (offline, 30 runs):** ~87% blocked, avg HC ~21% (was 91.7% on V0.2 via API).

**API inject path:** blocked at verify (403) before scoring.

---

### Background: what Qmodel V0.2 blocks

Qmodel V0.2 was trained after an adversarial patch cycle and includes:

1. **Static heuristic — “Procedural human-mimic movement signature”** (`backend/model.py`):
   - `straightness < 0.22`
   - `jitter_ratio > 0.28`
   - `0.28 < velocity_mean < 0.58`
   - `velocity_max < 2.5`
   - `click_dwell >= 90 ms`
   - `event_count > 15`
   - `duration > 4000 ms`
   - Adds **+0.32** heuristic bot score

2. **Dynamic rule — `evasion_cycle_001`** (`backend/qmodels/qmodel_v0.2_evasion_rules.json`):
   - Derived from the prior sharepad Bezier bot’s winning feature fingerprint
   - Matches narrow bands (e.g. straightness 0.17–0.33, jitter ≥0.29, vel_mean 0.25–0.49, duration ≥8998 ms, events ≥552)
   - Adds **+0.34** heuristic boost when all conditions hit

3. **ML classifier** on top of extracted features (velocity, jerk, straightness, etc.)

The **old Bezier/sharepad bot** (`test/test_best_config.py`) scored only **~32% max** on Qmodel V0.2 (avg ~23%) because it landed inside these patched bands.

