## Issue 002 — Qmodel V0.3 live Playwright button-sequence evasion (74%)

**Status:** patched (Qmodel V0.4 + kinematic hardening); open (further Playwright tuning)  
**Date:** 2026-08-17  
**Target model:** `qmodel_v0.3` (latest)  
**Challenge:** `button_sequence`  
**Goal:** ≥70% human confidence, **no replay**, live canvas pointer recording  
**Constraint:** 20-minute timer; stopped early on success  
**Artifacts:** `test/timed_v03_live_solver.py`, `test/timed_v03_live_log.txt`, `test/timed_v03_live_result.json`

---

### Summary

Live Playwright mouse on the dashboard (`#challenge-canvas` pointer listeners → `/api/challenge/verify`) reached **74% human confidence** (`PASSED: HUMAN`) against **Qmodel V0.3** in **9 attempts / ~40s** on the winning family (`os_direct_v2`). No event-JSON replay, no `/api/verify` inject, no dashboard Linear/Bezier/Humanoid `run-bot` path.

This closes the “live browser ≥70%” gap left open in Issue 001 (best prior live score was **60%** on V0.2). Patched in **Qmodel V0.4** (see Blue-team patch below).

---

### Constraints and scoring path

Dashboard strict mode (`CAPTCHA_STRICT=1`) requires:

- `source: "dashboard"` + session `verify_token`
- Pointer attestation (`pid` / `pt` / `src` from real PointerEvents)
- Wall-clock vs telemetry duration (blocks instant JSON inject)
- Open `/api/verify` disabled

Therefore the only viable path was **live `page.mouse` on Chromium** against `http://127.0.0.1:8010/`, same backend as the Cursor dashboard tab. The Cursor IDE browser cannot dispatch CDP `Input.*`, so discrete MCP clicks were not used for scoring. Dashboard **Humanoid/Bezier/Linear** buttons call `/api/challenge/run-bot` (server-generated bot telemetry, already in V0.3 training as bot) and were not used.

Scoring uses **max-risk over dynamic active windows** (`backend/main.py` `_evaluate_events_dynamic`). Any single bot-looking burst can tank the session.

V0.3 bands that had to be **missed** (heuristic #9 / #10 + `evasion_cycle_002`):

- #9 wobble-linear: jitter `<0.13`, vel_mean `0.60–1.08`, vel_max `3.2–10`, dwell `60–115ms`, events `180–540`, duration `3400–9500ms`, straightness `<0.56`
- #10: straightness `<0.22`, jitter `<0.14`, vel_mean `>0.68`, events `>175`, duration `>3200`, dwell `55–115`
- Dynamic cycle 002: jitter `≤0.14`, vel_mean `0.60–1.08`, dwell `≥55`, duration `≥3200`, events `≥175`, straightness `≤0.56`
- Also avoid: straightness `>0.985`, vel_max `>15`, dwell `<15ms`, constant speed, zero jitter

---

### What was tried (dead / weak runs)

Human desktop windows from `datasets/human/input_log_20260812_171705_to_20260812_171721.csv` (4 windows) were used as a kinematic compass — not as replay:

| Feature | Human p10–p90 (that file) |
|---------|---------------------------|
| vel_mean | 1.32–2.65 px/ms |
| jerk_mean | 0.41–0.56 |
| acc_mean | 0.59–0.71 |
| jitter | 0.23–0.32 |
| straightness | 0.51–0.62 |

Playwright’s ~8ms hop floor makes true 1px/1ms OS sampling hard; later families approximated it with **large steps + `asyncio.sleep(0)`**.

| Family / script | Method | Typical HC | Events | Why it failed |
|-----------------|--------|------------|--------|----------------|
| Existing `test/qmodel_v03_humanoid_playwright.py` | Min-jerk Fitts profiles | 0–9% (prior log max 9%) | ~80–260 | Humanoid simulated is ~99.8% bot in V0.3 training |
| `timed_v03` v1 sparse (`slow_arc` / `careful` / `busy_mouse`) | Eased arc, 7–16px spacing, slow vel | max **18%** (`jitter_arc` 182 ev) | 105–258 | vel_mean too low vs human; ML reject; **no heuristic flags** |
| `timed_v03` v2 dense + fidget | 2.6–5.5px spacing, wander/fidget, 400ms-ish pauses | 6–15% | 457–837 | Extra bursts still look like challenge-bots; max-risk windowing hurts |
| `os_wiggly` | Large sine arc | 14–50% (one **60% PASSED**) | 113–261 | Straightness often ~0.01–0.18; inconsistent |
| `os_fast` | Faster hops, moderate arc | 3–38% | 102–173 | vel closer to 0.8–1.0 but jitter/str not in the passing cluster |
| `os_direct` (no micro-samples) | Larger steps, smaller arc | **54% PASSED** once, then 2–9% | ~103–121 | Lucky vel=1.19; not repeatable |

v1/v2 were killed mid-run (exit 4294967295) after it was clear they could not hit 70%.

---

### What worked — `os_direct_v2`

**Script:** `test/timed_v03_live_solver.py`  
**Browser:** Playwright Chromium headless, viewport 1440×960  
**Model select:** `#active-model` = `qmodel_v0.3`  
**Challenge select:** `#challenge-type` = `button_sequence`  
**Flow:** click New Challenge → live mouse along `spec.sequence` → canvas auto-submit / Submit → read `#human-confidence`

**Motion (no replay):**

1. Start in the challenge area (random offset).
2. For each button: cosine-eased chord + perpendicular sine arc (`arc_px` 22–55) + Gaussian tremor.
3. Step size mixed: 18% tiny (2–6px) else 18–42px (high `velocity_std`).
4. After each hop: **1–3 one-pixel jiggles** with `sleep(0)` (raises jitter into ~0.70–0.79; lifts jerk/acc slightly).
5. Rare 12–40ms stall (5%); short inter-button pause 40–120ms.
6. Click: aim Gaussian σ 1.4–2.4px, dwell 30–70ms, optional 1px press wobble.

**Config (`sample_cfg` / `os_direct_v2`):**

```
step_px:     18–42
speed_px_ms: 1.40–2.60   (hint only; v2 mostly sleep(0))
arc_px:      22–55
tremor_px:   0.8–1.6
aim_sigma:   1.4–2.4
dwell_s:     0.03–0.07
pause_s:     0.04–0.12
```

---

### Winning run

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| **Human confidence** | **74%** |
| Decision | PASSED: HUMAN |
| Family | `os_direct_v2` |
| Attempt | 9 (of that restart; ~40s wall) |
| Events | 163 |
| Flags | none |
| velocity_mean | 0.6014 |
| jerk_mean | 0.0620 |
| acceleration_mean | 0.1428 |
| jitter_ratio | 0.7888 |
| straightness_index | 0.2683 |

Same restart, all **PASSED** before the win: 69%, 60%, 64%, 58%, 63%, 60%, 56%, 61%, **74%**. Attempt 02 had `Abnormal velocity spike (34.8 px/ms)` but still 60% PASSED (spike heuristic +0.40, ML still under the combined cap enough to pass).

**Why this evaded V0.3 heuristics:** jitter **0.79** is far above cycle-002 / #9 (`<0.13–0.14`). vel_mean **0.60** sits on the #9 lower edge but #9 also needs jitter `<0.13` (miss). Event count 163 is below cycle-002 `≥175`. Dwell ~30–70ms is often below #9’s `≥60`. The RF then assigned relatively low bot probability on that window set.

**Why it is not the Issue 001 wobble bot:** that winner had jitter **0.07** and vel_mean **0.78** — exactly the band V0.3 patched. This live bot is the opposite on jitter (very high) and uses Playwright-native timestamps.

---

### Run command

```bash
python test/timed_v03_live_solver.py
```

Requires dashboard at `http://127.0.0.1:8010/` with `qmodel_v0.3` loadable.

