## Issue 003 — Qmodel V0.4 live Playwright button-sequence evasion (78%)

**Status:** patched (Qmodel V0.5 + kinematic hardening); open (further Playwright families)  
**Date:** 2026-08-17  
**Target model:** `qmodel_v0.4` (latest)  
**Challenge:** `button_sequence`  
**Goal:** ≥70% human confidence, **no replay**, live canvas pointer recording  
**Constraint:** 20-minute timer; stopped early on success  
**Artifacts:** `test/timed_v04_live_solver.py`, `test/timed_v04_live_log.txt`, `test/timed_v04_live_result.json`

---

### Summary

Live Playwright mouse on the dashboard reached **78% human confidence** (`PASSED: HUMAN`) against **Qmodel V0.4** on **attempt 1 / ~5s** using family `hi_dyn`. No replay, no API inject, no dashboard Linear/Bezier/Humanoid `run-bot`.

This evades the Issue 002 patch: V0.4 heuristics **#11–#14**, dynamic rule **`evasion_cycle_003`**, and hop+jiggle training data. The old `os_direct_v2` 1px-jiggle fingerprint is blocked; this run used **alternating large/small steps**, **no micro-scribble**, and **higher mean velocity**.

---

### What V0.4 blocks (Issue 002 patch)

Static heuristics in `backend/model.py`:

| # | Flag | Core AND-conditions | Boost |
|---|------|---------------------|-------|
| 11 | Playwright micro-jiggle inflation | jitter `>0.48`, jerk `<0.18`, acc `<0.28`, vel `0.42–0.88`, events `85–320`, str `<0.52`, duration `>2000` | +0.48 |
| 12 | Automation kinematic mismatch | jitter `>0.38`, jerk `<0.22`, acc `<0.35`, vel `<0.92`, events `70–380`, duration `>1800` | +0.36 |
| 13 | Inflated jitter sparse-hop | jitter `>0.50`, vel `<0.88`, events `<280`, str `<0.55` | +0.40 |
| 14 | Extreme jitter inflation | jitter `>0.62`, events `<300`, str `<0.55` | +0.52 |

Dynamic `evasion_cycle_003` (`backend/qmodels/qmodel_v0.4_evasion_rules.json`): jitter `≥0.639`, jerk `≤0.162`, acc `≤0.263`, vel `0.451–0.751`, events `158–243`, str `0.188–0.348`, dwell `≥60`, duration `≥3000`, vel_max `≤6` → +0.34.

Issue 002 winner (`os_direct_v2`: jitter ~0.79, vel ~0.60, jerk ~0.06, acc ~0.14, events ~163) hits **#11+#12+#13+#14** and cycle 003. Post-patch that profile scores **0% HC**.

---

### Method — `hi_dyn` (no 1px jiggle)

**Script:** `test/timed_v04_live_solver.py`  
**Browser:** Playwright Chromium headless, viewport 1440×960  
**Model:** `#active-model` = `qmodel_v0.4`  
**Challenge:** `#challenge-type` = `button_sequence`  
**Flow:** New Challenge → live `page.mouse` along `spec.sequence` → canvas auto-submit → read `#human-confidence`

**Motion (no replay):**

1. Random start in the challenge area.
2. Per button: cosine-eased chord + modest perpendicular sine arc (`arc_px` 14–32) + light Gaussian tremor (~0.9px).
3. **Alternate** large hops (22–48px) and small hops (4–9px) so `velocity_std` / acc stay non-flat — **not** clustered 1px scribbles.
4. Occasional 4–10px along-path correction (`correct_p` 0.22).
5. `asyncio.sleep(0)` between hops (Playwright ~8ms floor sets dt).
6. Click: aim σ ~2px, dwell 45–85ms; short pause 50–140ms between buttons.

**Config (`hi_dyn`):**

```
step_px:    22–48
small_px:   4–9
arc_px:     14–32
tremor_px:  0.9
aim_sigma:  2.0
dwell_s:    0.045–0.085
pause_s:    0.05–0.14
alt_steps:  True
correct_p:  0.22
ease:       True
```

Other families in the same script (not needed this run): `straighter`, `fast_human`, `dense_path`.

---

### Winning run

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| **Human confidence** | **78%** |
| Decision | PASSED: HUMAN |
| Family | `hi_dyn` |
| Attempt | **1** (~5.0 s wall) |
| Events | 141 |
| Heuristic score | **0.00** |
| Flags | none |
| velocity_mean | **1.0798** |
| jerk_mean | 0.0558 |
| acceleration_mean | 0.1699 |
| jitter_ratio | 0.4029 |
| straightness_index | 0.3107 |

**Why this missed V0.4 bands:**

| Rule | Miss reason |
|------|-------------|
| #11 | vel_mean **1.08** not in `0.42–0.88`; jitter **0.40** not `>0.48` |
| #12 | vel_mean **1.08** not `<0.92` (jitter 0.40 would otherwise match `>0.38`) |
| #13 | vel_mean not `<0.88`; jitter not `>0.50` |
| #14 | jitter **0.40** not `>0.62` |
| cycle 003 | jitter not `≥0.639`; vel not in `0.45–0.75`; events 141 `<158` |

Jerk/acc remain low (similar to Issue 002), but V0.4 gated those checks behind **high jitter and/or low velocity**. Raising vel_mean above **0.92** and keeping jitter **~0.40** (human desktop was ~0.23–0.32; Issue 002 win was ~0.79) is enough to zero the heuristic stack; ML then scored the window set as human.

**Contrast with Issue 002 `os_direct_v2`:**

| | Issue 002 win (V0.3) | Issue 003 win (V0.4) |
|--|----------------------|----------------------|
| Extra samples | 1–3 **1px jiggles** per hop | none |
| Step pattern | mixed 2–6px / 18–42px | **alternating** 22–48 / 4–9 |
| jitter | ~0.79 | **0.40** |
| vel_mean | ~0.60 | **1.08** |
| HC vs V0.4 | 0% (patched) | **78%** |

